  "note": "Size and SHA-256 pins for the companion Rust bundle `woof global fetch-doors` stages into ~/.woof/global-doors, beside the engine's own bundle rather than inside it.  The bundle carries exactly the doors `arwen_global.doors.doors_from_bundle('gpuwm-global')` names: six binaries no published gpuwm bridge bundle carries at all (rw_atms, rw_gnssro, rw_ndbc, rw_igra2, rw_amv, rw_wis2), and two the engine's bundle carries under the same filename in an older build that has none of the subcommands this package calls (rw_asos, rw_goes).  This file is written by tools/build_door_bundle.py from the exact bytes a release published, never by hand.  `platforms` is empty until the first release is cut, and `woof global fetch-doors` reports that as 'no companion bundle has been published yet' rather than inventing a download URL.  If the engine takes those crates onto its own line, this file goes empty permanently and every door resolves from `woof fetch-bridges`.",
